    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1082">

                <pb facs="0896" n="886" sameAs="frus:frus1949v08/pg886"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00B/6–2349: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Dairen</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Paddock</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dairen</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-06-23T13:00:00+09:00">June 23, 1949—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:37 p. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>181. Workers of all ranks in all Soviet and Chinese Communist trusts must attend
                    “political studies” classes several hours each week after work. It understood
                    Mukden American Consulate spy story currently being stressed at these classes to
                    emphasize every American Consulate “nest of spies” and to warn Soviets and
                    Chinese against any contact with this Consulate.</p>
                <p>Recently Soviet clerk in Soviet department store (Churin) chatted with Consulate
                    officer about 5 minutes during purchase. After latter <pb facs="0897" n="887"
                        xml:id="pg887"/> left two Soviet Kommandatura officers reprimanded clerk for
                    being friendly to “our enemy” and threatened punishment if repeated.</p>
                <p>Sent Nanking 132; repeated Department 181, Canton 75, Shanghai 152, Moscow
                    102.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paddock</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
